> Edit: My current workaround is to use an `[Export]` variable for the scene's file path instead:
> 
> [Export(PropertyHint.File)] public string MyScenePath { get; private set; }

Face same problem and also rewrite logic to handle path BUT after loading scene and queuing it free after some time textures still in VRAM.

So in my project i load default parallax2D background with option to change it.
After manually clicking on all options VRAM usage goes from 60 to 460 Mb.

C# method that handle reloading:
```csharp
    void SetEnvironment(int sceneIdx)
    {
        if (EnvironmentContainer.GetChildCount() != 0)
        {
            var _bg = EnvironmentContainer.GetChild(0);
            EnvironmentContainer.RemoveChild(_bg);
            _bg.QueueFree();
        }

        EnvironmentContainer.AddChild(
            ResourceLoader.Load<PackedScene>(BackgroundsScenePaths[sceneIdx]).Instantiate<Node2D>()
        );
    }
```

Did you face overusing VRAM in this case? Or did it .NET specific thing?
